window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-c369cec5f3b8338d"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"prisma-airs\">Prisma AIRS</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引见 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>将 Palo Alto Networks Prisma AIRS 连接到 Codex，可以在提示词送达模型之前应用你的安全策略。工作区管理员只需为整个工作区配置一次集成。</p> <p>Prisma AIRS 可以应用你在安全配置文件中设置的防护措施，例如数据丢失防护、提示词注入检测和恶意 URL 检测。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">开始之前</h2> <p>你需要：</p> <ul> <li>已启用 Prisma AIRS 访问权限的 ChatGPT 工作区。如需申请访问权限，请联系你的 OpenAI 客户团队。</li> <li>工作区管理员权限。</li> <li>Prisma AIRS API 密钥、已配置的安全配置文件，以及部署所用的服务端点。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"connect-prisma-airs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"prisma-airs_1\">连接 Prisma AIRS</h2> <ol> <li>以工作区管理员身份打开 <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin Console（需联网）</a>，然后选择你的工作区。</li> <li>在 <strong>Policy &amp; security（策略与安全）</strong>下选择 <strong>External guardrails（外部防护）</strong>，找到 <strong>Prisma AIRS</strong>。如果没有该选项，请联系 OpenAI 客户团队为你的工作区启用访问权限。</li> <li>输入 <strong>API key（API 密钥）</strong>、<strong>Security profile（安全配置文件）</strong>名称或 ID，以及 <strong>Endpoint URL（端点 URL）</strong>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Enforcement mode（强制模式）</strong>，以及 <strong>On AIRS failure（AIRS 发生故障时）</strong>的处理方式。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Save connection（保存连接）</strong>。Codex 会验证连接并加密你的 API 密钥。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Test connection（测试连接）</strong>，验证已保存的配置。</li> <li>开启 <strong>Enable Prisma AIRS（启用 Prisma AIRS）</strong>，开始扫描整个工作区的提示词。</li> </ol> <p>保存连接并不会启用扫描；你还必须开启 <strong>Enable Prisma AIRS</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-an-endpoint\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择端点</h2> <p>使用适用于你的 Prisma AIRS 部署且已获批准的端点：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>区域</th> <th>端点</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>美国</td> <td><code>https://service.api.aisecurity.paloaltonetworks.com</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>德国</td> <td><code>https://service-de.api.aisecurity.paloaltonetworks.com</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>印度</td> <td><code>https://service-in.api.aisecurity.paloaltonetworks.com</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>新加坡</td> <td><code>https://service-sg.api.aisecurity.paloaltonetworks.com</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Codex 默认使用美国端点。工作区的数据驻留要求可能会限制你可使用的端点。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-how-to-handle-prompts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">选择提示词的处理方式</h2> <p><strong>Enforcement mode（强制模式）</strong>决定 Prisma AIRS 标记提示词时的处理方式：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Block（阻止）</strong>：在提示词送达模型前将其拦截。这是默认选项。</li> <li><strong>Alert only（仅告警）</strong>：记录检测结果，但允许提示词继续处理。</li> </ul> <p><strong>On AIRS failure（AIRS 发生故障时）</strong>决定 Prisma AIRS 不可用或未响应时的处理方式：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Allow prompts（允许提示词）</strong>：即使扫描尚未完成，也继续处理。这是默认选项。</li> <li><strong>Block prompts（阻止提示词）</strong>：阻止提示词，直到 Prisma AIRS 能够完成扫描。</li> </ul> <p>如果你的安全策略要求每条纳入扫描范围的提示词都必须获得扫描判定，请选择 <strong>Block prompts</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"understand-what-gets-scanned\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">了解扫描范围</h2> <p>当用户通过配置好的 ChatGPT 工作区身份验证时，Codex 会将新提交的提示词文本发送到已配置的 Prisma AIRS 端点进行检查。该配置覆盖的 Codex 工作流包括桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展和云端。使用 Platform API 密钥进行身份验证的会话不受此配置覆盖。有关要求用户使用指定登录方式和工作区，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=enforce-a-login-method-or-workspace\">强制登录方式或工作区</a>。</p> <p>此集成不会让 Prisma AIRS 扫描助手回复、工具调用、工具结果、文件或图片。Prisma AIRS 能检测哪些威胁和敏感数据，由你配置的安全配置文件决定。</p> <p>Codex 会加密你的 API 密钥，并且保存后不会再次显示。启用提示词检查前，请查看 Palo Alto Networks 的数据处理、保留和驻留政策。这些政策适用于发送到 Prisma AIRS 的提示词。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-the-connection\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">管理连接</h2> <p>返回 <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin Console（需联网）</a>，选择你的工作区，然后打开 <strong>Policy &amp; security（策略与安全）</strong> &gt; <strong>External guardrails（外部防护）</strong>来管理集成：</p> <ul> <li>选择 <strong>Test connection（测试连接）</strong>，验证已保存的 API 密钥、安全配置文件和端点。</li> <li>输入新密钥并选择 <strong>Rotate API key（轮换 API 密钥）</strong>，即可在不更改其他设置的情况下替换已保存的密钥。</li> <li>关闭 <strong>Enable Prisma AIRS（启用 Prisma AIRS）</strong>，即可停止扫描并保留已保存的配置。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Disconnect（断开连接）</strong>并确认，即可停止扫描并删除已保存的连接和 API 密钥。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"disable-or-disconnect-without-a-sidebar-entry\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">没有侧边栏入口时如何停用或断开连接</h3> <p>如果已保存配置的工作区中没有显示 <strong>External guardrails（外部防护）</strong>，工作区管理员可以打开有限的恢复视图：<code>https://admin.openai.com/workspace/&lt;workspace-id&gt;/external-guardrails</code>。 将 <code>&lt;workspace-id&gt;</code> 替换为 Admin Console URL 中的工作区 ID。</p> <p>在此视图中，你可以查看已保存的配置、关闭 <strong>Enable Prisma AIRS</strong>，或选择 <strong>Disconnect</strong> 并确认。此视图不支持设置、修改配置、测试连接、轮换密钥或重新启用集成。请联系 OpenAI 客户团队恢复配置访问权限。</p> <p>有关更全面的工作区设置和策略管理，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员部署指南</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"prisma-airs\">Prisma AIRS</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Connect Palo Alto Networks Prisma AIRS to apply your security policies to Codex prompts before they reach the model. Workspace admins configure the integration once for their workspace.</p> <p>Prisma AIRS can apply the protections configured in your security profile, such as data loss prevention, prompt injection detection, and malicious URL detection.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h2> <p>You need:</p> <ul> <li>A ChatGPT workspace with Prisma AIRS access enabled. Contact your OpenAI account team to request access.</li> <li>Workspace administrator permissions.</li> <li>A Prisma AIRS API key, a configured security profile, and the service endpoint for your deployment.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"connect-prisma-airs\">Connect Prisma AIRS</h2> <ol> <li>Open <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin Console (online)</a> as a workspace administrator and select your workspace.</li> <li>Under <strong>Policy &amp; security</strong>, select <strong>External guardrails</strong> and find <strong>Prisma AIRS</strong>. If this entry isn't available, ask your OpenAI account team to enable access for your workspace.</li> <li>Enter your <strong>API key</strong>, <strong>Security profile</strong> name or ID, and <strong>Endpoint URL</strong>.</li> <li>Choose an <strong>Enforcement mode</strong> and the behavior <strong>On AIRS failure</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Save connection</strong>. Codex validates the connection and encrypts your API key.</li> <li>Select <strong>Test connection</strong> to verify the saved configuration.</li> <li>Turn on <strong>Enable Prisma AIRS</strong> to start scanning prompts across the workspace.</li> </ol> <p>Saving the connection doesn't enable scanning. You must also turn on <strong>Enable Prisma AIRS</strong>.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-an-endpoint\">Choose an endpoint</h2> <p>Use the approved endpoint for your Prisma AIRS deployment:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Region</th> <th>Endpoint</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>United States</td> <td><code>https://service.api.aisecurity.paloaltonetworks.com</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Germany</td> <td><code>https://service-de.api.aisecurity.paloaltonetworks.com</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>India</td> <td><code>https://service-in.api.aisecurity.paloaltonetworks.com</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Singapore</td> <td><code>https://service-sg.api.aisecurity.paloaltonetworks.com</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Codex uses the United States endpoint by default. Workspace data-residency requirements can restrict which endpoint you can use.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-how-to-handle-prompts\">Choose how to handle prompts</h2> <p><strong>Enforcement mode</strong> determines what happens when Prisma AIRS flags a prompt:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Block</strong>: Stop the prompt before it reaches the model. This is the default.</li> <li><strong>Alert only</strong>: Record the detection and allow the prompt to continue.</li> </ul> <p><strong>On AIRS failure</strong> determines what happens if Prisma AIRS is unavailable or doesn't respond:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Allow prompts</strong>: Continue without a completed scan. This is the default.</li> <li><strong>Block prompts</strong>: Stop the prompt until Prisma AIRS can scan it.</li> </ul> <p>Choose <strong>Block prompts</strong> when your security policy requires every covered prompt to receive a scan decision.</p> <h2 id=\"understand-what-gets-scanned\">Understand what gets scanned</h2> <p>Codex sends newly submitted prompt text to the configured Prisma AIRS endpoint for inspection. This applies to covered Codex workflows, including the app, CLI, IDE extension, and cloud, when users authenticate to the configured ChatGPT workspace. Sessions authenticated with a Platform API key aren't covered. See <a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=enforce-a-login-method-or-workspace\">Enforce a login method or workspace</a> to require the intended sign-in method and workspace.</p> <p>Prisma AIRS doesn't scan assistant responses, tool calls, tool results, files, or images through this integration. Your configured security profile determines which threats and sensitive data Prisma AIRS detects.</p> <p>Codex encrypts your API key and never displays it after you save it. Review Palo Alto Networks' data-handling, retention, and residency policies before enabling prompt inspection. Those policies apply to prompts sent to Prisma AIRS.</p> <h2 id=\"manage-the-connection\">Manage the connection</h2> <p>Return to <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin Console (online)</a>, select your workspace, and open <strong>Policy &amp; security</strong> &gt; <strong>External guardrails</strong> to manage the integration:</p> <ul> <li>Select <strong>Test connection</strong> to verify your saved API key, security profile, and endpoint.</li> <li>Enter a new key and select <strong>Rotate API key</strong> to replace the saved key without changing the other settings.</li> <li>Turn off <strong>Enable Prisma AIRS</strong> to stop scanning while preserving the saved configuration.</li> <li>Select <strong>Disconnect</strong>, then confirm, to stop scanning and delete the saved connection and API key.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"disable-or-disconnect-without-a-sidebar-entry\">Disable or disconnect without a sidebar entry</h3> <p>If <strong>External guardrails</strong> doesn't appear for a workspace with a saved configuration, a workspace administrator can open the limited recovery view at <code>https://admin.openai.com/workspace/&lt;workspace-id&gt;/external-guardrails</code>. Replace <code>&lt;workspace-id&gt;</code> with the workspace ID from your Admin Console URL.</p> <p>This view lets you see the saved configuration, turn off <strong>Enable Prisma AIRS</strong>, or select <strong>Disconnect</strong> and confirm. It doesn't allow setup, configuration changes, connection testing, key rotation, or turning the integration back on. Contact your OpenAI account team to restore configuration access.</p> <p>For broader workspace setup and policy management, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a>.</p>"};
